### MediCitas — RF5 horarios + RF6 bloqueos
### Requiere: docker compose up (api :8080, keycloak :6767)
### Permiso: adm-clinica o profesional (solo propios)

@host = http://localhost:8080
@kc = http://localhost:6767
@realm = medicitas
@client = api

### Token adm clínica norte
# @name tokenAdm
POST {{kc}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client}}&username=adm-norte&password={{$dotenv SEED_USER_PASSWORD}}&grant_type=password

### Listar profesionales (para copiar un id)
GET {{host}}/profesionales
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}

@profesionalId = {{$guid}}
# Sustituir @profesionalId por un id real de GET /profesionales

### RF5 — listar horarios (I5: clinicaId en query se ignora)
GET {{host}}/profesionales/{{profesionalId}}/horarios?clinicaId=clinica-sur
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}

### RF5 — crear bloque (lunes 09:00–12:00)
POST {{host}}/profesionales/{{profesionalId}}/horarios
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "diaSemana": 1,
  "horaInicio": "09:00",
  "horaFin": "12:00",
  "vigenteDesde": "2026-01-01",
  "vigenteHasta": null
}

### RF5 — desactivar horario
# @name horarioCreado
PATCH {{host}}/horarios/{{horarioId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "activo": false
}

### RF6 — listar bloqueos
GET {{host}}/profesionales/{{profesionalId}}/bloqueos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}

### RF6 — crear bloqueo (responde conflictos de citas reservadas; no las cancela)
POST {{host}}/profesionales/{{profesionalId}}/bloqueos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "inicio": "2026-11-20T09:00:00-06:00",
  "fin": "2026-11-20T17:00:00-06:00",
  "motivo": "Vacaciones"
}

### RF6 — eliminar bloqueo
DELETE {{host}}/bloqueos/{{bloqueoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdm.response.body.access_token}}

### Token profesional (solo agenda propia)
# @name tokenProf
POST {{kc}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client}}&username=dra-garcia&password={{$dotenv SEED_USER_PASSWORD}}&grant_type=password
